# A Tribute to the Professor of Drama!

An excellent celebration honouring Pammal Sambandhanar, the Professor of Drama, was held on the first of this month at Kala Mandapam in Triplicane, Madras. Many people participated in this event conducted by the Drama Association, without regard to party rivalry.

In the morning, the Professor of Drama was brought in procession from the Suguna Vilasa Sabha on Mount Road, surrounded by artists. Chief Minister Rajaji draped him with a golden shawl. Dr. C. P. Ramaswami presided. Thiru. Vi. Ka. inaugurated a library.

Comrades M. P. Sivagnanam, Muthiah of Chettinad, T. K. Shanmugam, P. Jeevanandham, V. V. Srinivasa Iyengar, Nawab Rajamanickam, M. R. Radha, Bhaktavatsalam, Mayor Chengalvarayan, Kothamangalam Subbu, K. S. Ramaswami, V. C. Gopalaratnam, actor Balachandar, Chinna Annamalai, Kannadasan, Anbazhagan, Kambadasan, and others spoke in praise of the Professor of Drama. Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam General Secretary Annadurai delivered an address.

Afterwards, numerous distinguished actors performed scenes from several plays written by the Professor of Drama. Comrades K. R. Ramaswami, the scholar of acting, S. S. Rajendran, M. R. Radha, T. S. Balaiah, Sampangi, T. R. Ramachandran, K. Sarangapani, and many others participated.

Kalaivanar N. S. Krishnan thanked everyone whose presence distinguished the celebration.

In the morning, a sweet nadaswaram performance by Kulikkarai Pichaippa was also held.

(*Dravida Nadu*, news item, 8-2-28)
